# The Docker build context is this directory (App Platform sets it from the
# component's source_dir), and `COPY . .` would otherwise sweep in whatever is
# lying around a developer's checkout.
#
# The dangerous one is .env.local: it is gitignored, so it never shows up in a
# diff, and it sets NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000 and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BILLING_LIVE=1. Next loads .env.local ahead of the process env,
# so a local or CI `docker build` would bake a production image whose every CTA
# points at localhost and whose pricing page links to live Stripe checkout —
# while the build-args we passed sit there, silently overridden. Keep .env.example
# (documentation only, never read by the build).
node_modules
.next
out
.env*
!.env.example
*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.gitignore
*.log
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
